
<p>Apple just <a href="https://9to5mac.com/2026/04/01/apple-studio-display-xdr-price-drop/">dropped the price of the VESA-mount Studio Display XDR by $400</a>. The standless version is now $2,899, down from $3,299. The stand version stays at $3,299.</p>



<p>That&#8217;s a big correction for a product that&#8217;s only been on the market for a few weeks. And it makes me curious about the internal conversations that led to it. Did the original pricing miss the mark? Were pre-order numbers lower than expected? Did someone at Apple realize that charging the same price for a monitor without a stand as one with a stand didn&#8217;t make a lot of sense?</p>



<p>Either way, if you are looking at the new monitor <em>sans</em> stand, it just got a bit more affordable.</p>
